<task id="030" project="field-mapping-server-write-path-r1">
  <metadata>
    <title>Office /api/office/todo and Office document save through the service, with the association set in the create (FR-18)</title>
    <phase>3 W3 Product creators onto the service</phase>
    <gate>019 complete</gate>
    <status>in-progress (030a done; 030b re-scoped below)</status>
    <rigor>FULL</rigor>
    <rigor-reason>Modifies .cs in Sprk.Bff.Api; tags include bff-api, office, documents; touches a worker that creates documents (data-mutation); adds tests at KEEP paths (TEST-MODIFYING override).</rigor-reason>
    <model-tier>opus</model-tier>
    <model-tier-reason>Document save is a two-step create-then-update flow with duplicate detection, SPE pointers and Service Bus retries; collapsing the association into the create needs careful judgment.</model-tier-reason>
    <effort>high</effort>
    <parallel-group>W3-server</parallel-group>
    <parallel-safe>true</parallel-safe>
    <deps>019</deps>
    <tags>bff-api, office, documents, testing</tags>
    <estimated-effort>8-12 hours</estimated-effort>
  </metadata>

  <prompt>Route `POST /api/office/todo` (`OfficeService.CreateTodoAsync`, `Services/Office/OfficeService.cs` ~:2092-2295) and Office document save (`OfficeDocumentPersistence.CreateDocumentWithSpePointersAsync` ~:124, `Workers/Office/UploadFinalizationWorker.cs` create-then-update ~:615-690) through `RecordCreationService`, with the document's association set IN the create request, not by a follow-up update (word gaps G1/G2). Office Invoice quick-create is already done in task 018.</prompt>
  <role>SPAARKE platform developer, .NET 10 BFF, Office add-in and SharePoint Embedded document persistence. Follow ADRs strictly.</role>
  <goal>An Office-created To Do and an Office-saved document each carry mapping (if profiled), I-1 stamp and record-first owner at create (no index column written by the server; the document stamp names the files index after indexing, FR-40); document save issues one create call carrying the association and no separate association update; Office contract tests pass unchanged.</goal>

  <context>
    <background>spec.md FR-18, FR-06/FR-07, NFR-07. Today `CreateTodoAsync` builds a `sprk_todo` entity, resolves its owner itself (`ResolveTodoOwnerTeamAsync`, owner set at ~:2285) and calls `_genericEntityService.CreateAsync` (~:2289). Document save creates the document via `_documentService.CreateDocumentAsync` (OfficeDocumentPersistence ~:283) and then updates it (~:287-330) with SPE pointers; the UploadFinalizationWorker also creates then updates, applying the association lookup in the update (`ApplyAssociationLookup`, ~:672). The worker's owner uses `ResolveDocumentOwnerTeamAsync` (~:121), where a CARRIED `OwningTeamId` wins (so email attachment children match their parent). The caller is the add-in user for the To Do (caller principal); for the worker the requesting user is carried in the payload (use the system principal with `RequestedBy` = the payload user, since the worker has no caller token).</background>
    <relevant-files>
      <file role="modify">src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/Services/Office/OfficeService.cs (CreateTodoAsync ~:2092; ResolveTodoOwnerTeamAsync, grep for the symbol)</file>
      <file role="modify">src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/Services/Office/OfficeDocumentPersistence.cs (CreateDocumentWithSpePointersAsync ~:124; create ~:283, update ~:287-330)</file>
      <file role="modify">src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/Workers/Office/UploadFinalizationWorker.cs (owner ~:121-140, create/update ~:615-690, ApplyAssociationLookup ~:1161)</file>
      <file role="modify">src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/Services/RecordCreation/RecordTableRules.cs (sprk_todo and sprk_document entries if a column default or exception is missing)</file>
      <file role="canonical-reference">src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/Services/RecordCreation/RecordCreationService.cs (tasks 013-016)</file>
      <file role="canonical-reference">tests/integration/contract/Api/Office/OfficeTodoRegardingContractTests.cs</file>
      <file role="canonical-reference">tests/integration/contract/Api/Office/OfficeTodoSourceAuthorizationContractTests.cs</file>
      <file role="canonical-reference">tests/integration/contract/Api/Office/OfficeSaveDocumentStampContractTests.cs</file>
      <file role="canonical-reference">tests/integration/data-mutation/OfficeVersionSave/ (grep for the document save tests)</file>
      <file role="new">tests/integration/data-mutation/RecordOwnership/OfficeDocumentCreateAssociationTests.cs (association in the create; one create call; no association update)</file>
    </relevant-files>
    <dependencies>
      <dependency task="019" status="required">W2 service deployed and reviewed.</dependency>
    </dependencies>
  </context>

  <constraints>
    <constraint source="ADR-008 (path A, spec ADR Tensions)">Scope: authorization. Office route filters stay; the To Do's payload-dependent checks (regarding record, document, communication carriers) run in `CallerWriteAuthorization` via the service; do not keep a private copy of those checks in OfficeService. The worker, having no caller token, uses the system principal and relies on the checks already done at the route that enqueued the job.</constraint>
    <constraint source="ADR-019">Scope: errors. The To Do and save endpoints keep their existing status codes and error codes (NFR-07); service refusals map to them through the Office adapter, unmapped kinds fail closed to the existing generic failure.</constraint>
    <constraint source="ADR-028">Scope: identity. To Do: caller principal (WhoAmI on the caller token inside the service). Worker: system principal with `RequestedBy` from the payload user; never impersonation; the create stays app-only.</constraint>
    <constraint source="ADR-010">Scope: DI. Use the already-registered scoped service; the worker obtains it from a scope created per message (as it does for other scoped services); no new registration.</constraint>
    <constraint source="ADR-036">Scope: worker. The UploadFinalizationWorker's retry/idempotency semantics are unchanged: a redelivered message must not create a second document (the existing content-duplicate detection ~:238 stays the guard), and the service create is not retried blindly after an ambiguous failure (NFR-03).</constraint>
    <constraint source="NFR-01 (spec)">Scope: Office paths. Fail closed: a refused or failed service call creates nothing and the existing error path runs; the carried `OwningTeamId` rule (email attachment children match their parent) is preserved as an explicit input to the service, not dropped.</constraint>
    <constraint source="project">Scope: no follow-up association update. The document's association lookup (matter/project/invoice/other direct slots, task 055's four slots) is a column in the create payload. SPE pointers that are only known after upload may remain a separate step ONLY if the pointer values cannot exist at create time; record that determination and its evidence in the task notes. The association must never depend on that update.</constraint>
    <constraint source="CLAUDE.md §10">Scope: BFF publish. Placement Justification in the PR; fresh-master publish-size delta per §10.4; `dotnet list package --vulnerable --include-transitive`; no package.</constraint>
    <constraint source="ADR-038">Scope: tests added or modified. KEEP paths; no Mock&lt;HttpMessageHandler&gt;; no DI-registration tests. Existing Office contract tests change only to follow a moved type, never by weakening an assertion. Cover the stated contract plus the named edge cases only.</constraint>
  </constraints>

  <knowledge>
    <topic>Office To Do and document save; SPE document persistence</topic>
    <files>
      <file>.claude/adr/ADR-002-thin-plugins.md</file>
