  <!-- ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
       030b: Office document save, re-scoped under the W3 direction (owner, reviewed by UAC-r2, 2026-11-06).
       Supersedes every document-save part of the prompt, goal, steps and acceptance criteria above.
       ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════ -->
  <subtask id="030b" status="in-progress">
    <title>Office document save: the association in the existing create call, pinned by guards (named exception to RecordCreationService)</title>
    <rigor>FULL</rigor>
    <direction source="notes/decisions.md 2026-11-06 W3 direction, bullet 030">
      The document save stays OUTSIDE RecordCreationService as a named exception: no given-id input, no pinned-owner input
      and no other change to the service. The association moves INTO the existing create call. Guards pin that only the
      server writes the narrowing and pointer columns, that the save calls the invariant-owner classes (stamp and owner),
      and that a given document id that already exists is refused, never updated.
    </direction>

    <scope>
      <in>The three Office sprk_document create sites: OfficeDocumentPersistence.CreateDocumentWithSpePointersAsync (the save),
        UploadFinalizationWorker.CreateDocumentRecordAsync (the worker's fallback create) and
        UploadFinalizationWorker.ProcessSingleAttachmentAsync (each attachment child).</in>
      <in>The shared create contract: CreateDocumentRequest gains one server-only ([JsonIgnore]) association member;
        DocumentAssociationMap gains a TryApply overload for the create; DataverseServiceClientImpl.CreateDocumentAsync stages
        it in the same create entity.</in>
      <out>RecordCreationService (no change); field mapping for Office documents (not applied: named exception);
        the version save and re-file paths; EmailAttachmentProcessor (not an Office path); the SPE pointer, email-archive and
        parent-document columns, which stay in the follow-up update (W3 ruling covers the association only).</out>
    </scope>

    <invariant-owners>
      <owner invariant="I-1 (stamp)">A document carries no stamp column: CoreAncestorResolver derives its root from its typed
        association column (CoreAncestorResolver.IntermediateRootColumns["sprk_document"]). The save's part of I-1 is writing
        that column in the create, through the one map (DocumentAssociationMap).</owner>
      <owner invariant="I-6 (owner)">IRecordOwnershipResolver.ResolveOwnerAsync over OfficeDocumentPersistence.DocumentOwnershipOf,
        asked over the same association the create writes; the worker's carried OwningTeamId still wins.</owner>
      <owner invariant="I-19 / task 189 / task 095 (narrowing)">OfficeDocumentPersistence.ApplyEmailCommunicationOutcome, the one
        setter of the create's narrowing members (unchanged).</owner>
    </invariant-owners>

    <acceptance-criteria>
      <criterion id="AC-1" testable="true">Save: CreateDocumentWithSpePointersAsync with a TargetEntity of a supported type makes
        exactly one CreateDocumentAsync call, whose request's Association names the column DocumentAssociationMap maps that type to
        and the target id, and exactly one UpdateDocumentAsync call, whose request sets none of the seven association lookups
        (Matter, Project, Invoice, WorkAssignment, Event, Todo, Contact). Covered for every accepted spelling (13).</criterion>
      <criterion id="AC-2" testable="true">Worker: the fallback create and each attachment child carry the payload's association in
        the create, and no UpdateDocumentAsync request from the worker sets an association lookup.</criterion>
      <criterion id="AC-3" testable="true">Staging: DataverseServiceClientImpl stages Association onto the created entity as
        [column] = EntityReference(target table, id) (sprk_matter to sprk_matter; event to sprk_relatedevent / sprk_event; contact to
        sprk_relatedcontact / contact); no Association writes no association column; an empty id is refused before any write.</criterion>
      <criterion id="AC-4" testable="true">Column agreement: for every spelling except contact, the create's column equals the
        column the owner question and the update path use (RecordReparent.ParentChangesOf over the update overload); contact maps to
        sprk_relatedcontact; every create column is in DocumentLinkFields.All with the same target; every matter / project / work
        assignment column is in CoreAncestorResolver.IntermediateRootColumns["sprk_document"].</criterion>
      <criterion id="AC-5" testable="true">Owner: the save's create carries the team it was handed; the worker's create carries the
        carried OwningTeamId when present (the resolver is not asked), and otherwise the team ResolveOwnerAsync returns for a
        question whose lookups hold the same association column and id as the create.</criterion>
      <criterion id="AC-6" testable="true">No index column (FR-40): no create or update request on these paths sets SearchIndexName,
        SearchIndexed or the index lifecycle dates.</criterion>
      <criterion id="AC-7" testable="true">Negative, unsupported type: an association type with no sprk_document column (account, an
        unknown string) or an empty id puts no association on the create and none on the update; the save still succeeds and the
        existing warning is logged (unchanged behaviour).</criterion>
      <criterion id="AC-8" testable="true">Negative, given id that already exists: when CreateDocumentAsync refuses the pre-assigned
        id (a duplicate-key fault), CreateDocumentWithSpePointersAsync throws and makes no UpdateDocumentAsync call: the existing
        row is never written. The save then takes its existing failure path.</criterion>
      <criterion id="AC-9" testable="true">Negative, wire: a JSON body naming association, id, owningTeamId, createdByPersonId,
        relatedCommunicationId, accessPermission, accessInheritanceRecord or restrictedBySubmission binds none of them onto
        CreateDocumentRequest.</criterion>
      <criterion id="AC-10" testable="true">No change to RecordCreationService, the worker's idempotency check, content dedup or the
        version-save path; no new endpoint, DI registration or package.</criterion>
      <criterion id="AC-11" testable="true">BFF build 0 errors / 0 warnings; filtered BFF tests (Office | RecordCreation |
        RecordOwnership) and tests/Spaarke.ArchTests pass. Existing Office suites pass unchanged except test fixtures that follow
        the association from the update to the create, with no assertion weakened.</criterion>
    </acceptance-criteria>

    <guards file="tests/Spaarke.ArchTests/OfficeDocumentSaveGuardTests.cs">
      <guard id="G1" name="association in the create">In OfficeDocumentPersistence.cs and UploadFinalizationWorker.cs, every
        DocumentAssociationMap.TryApply / ApplyAssociationLookup target is a CreateDocumentRequest, no association lookup property
        is set, and at least 3 apply sites are found.
        <must-fire>TryApply on an UpdateDocumentRequest; updateRequest.MatterLookup = id; an initializer setting ProjectLookup.</must-fire>
        <must-not-fire>TryApply on a new CreateDocumentRequest; on a parameter typed CreateDocumentRequest; a commented-out update apply.</must-not-fire></guard>
      <guard id="G2" name="the create stages the association">DataverseServiceClientImpl.CreateDocumentAsync calls
        StageDocumentAssociation(document, request).
        <must-fire>a body without the call; the call in another method; a commented-out call.</must-fire>
        <must-not-fire>a body with the call.</must-not-fire></guard>
      <guard id="G3" name="the save calls the owner class">OfficeService.cs and UploadFinalizationWorker.cs ask ResolveOwnerAsync over
        OfficeDocumentPersistence.DocumentOwnershipOf (at least 2 and 1 sites), and every Office create request sets OwningTeamId in
        its initializer.
        <must-fire>a create request without OwningTeamId; a file whose owner question is not built by DocumentOwnershipOf.</must-fire>
        <must-not-fire>a create request with OwningTeamId; ResolveOwnerAsync(OfficeDocumentPersistence.DocumentOwnershipOf(...) with {...}).</must-not-fire></guard>
      <guard id="G4" name="only the server writes the narrowing and pointer columns">CreateDocumentRequest's members without
        [JsonIgnore] are exactly Name, ContainerId and Description; the Office save body (SaveRequest and the types it carries) has no
        member named for a pointer, narrowing, owner or new-document id (ExistingDocumentId is the version-save target and is allowed).
        <must-fire>a type with a server-only member lacking [JsonIgnore]; a body type with a GraphItemId or AccessPermission member.</must-fire>
        <must-not-fire>the same types with the attribute / without those members.</must-not-fire></guard>
      <guard id="G5" name="a given id is created, never upserted">DataverseServiceClientImpl.CreateDocumentAsync creates with
        CreateAsync and has no Upsert; in server code only OfficeDocumentPersistence.cs sets Id in a CreateDocumentRequest initializer;
        every assignment of preAssignedDocumentId in OfficeService.cs is Guid.NewGuid() or null.
        <must-fire>a body with UpsertAsync or an UpsertRequest; a CreateDocumentRequest initializer with Id in another file;
          preAssignedDocumentId = request.Document.Id.</must-fire>
        <must-not-fire>a body with CreateAsync; preAssignedDocumentId = Guid.NewGuid().</must-not-fire></guard>
    </guards>

    <tests>
      <file role="new">tests/integration/data-mutation/RecordOwnership/OfficeDocumentCreateAssociationTests.cs (AC-1, 2, 5, 6, 7, 8)</file>
      <file role="new">tests/unit/domain/Dataverse/DocumentAssociationCreateStagingTests.cs (AC-3, 4, 9)</file>
      <file role="new">tests/Spaarke.ArchTests/OfficeDocumentSaveGuardTests.cs (G1-G5)</file>
      <file role="modify">tests/integration/contract/Api/Office/OfficeEndpointsContractTests.cs (the fake world reads the association from the create)</file>
    </tests>

    <known-limits>
      <limit>No field mapping on Office-saved documents (named exception; FR-18's "mapping if profiled" does not hold for them).</limit>
      <limit>The pointer, email-archive and parent-document columns stay in the follow-up update; a failure between the create and
        that update leaves a row with its association, owner and narrowing but without its pointer (unchanged).</limit>
      <limit>Guards G1, G3 and G5 are source scans: they see the shapes their controls pin, not every possible spelling.</limit>
    </known-limits>
  </subtask>

  <execution><skill>.claude/skills/task-execute/SKILL.md</skill></execution>
</task>
